From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Cattrall <krazyjakee@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:18:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dioxus-native: draw on the CPU where there's no usable GPU

The gpu-cpu-fallback feature builds vello_hybrid and vello_cpu (over
softbuffer) and picks at run time: vello_hybrid, refusing software
adapters; when it can't start (no adapter, device or surface, or only
llvmpipe, lavapipe or WARP) the window switches to vello_cpu on the same
window, which repaints only damage. RendererOptions::cpu_only skips the
GPU. DioxusNativeWindowRenderer::is_cpu and fallback_reason say which is
drawing, so an app can lighten its look.

Both backends paint through anyrender's DynScenePainter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
